# CakePHP Ignis
{% if assist.hasMcpEnabled() %}

## Tools
- CakePHP Ignis is an MCP server with tools designed for this application. Prefer Ignis tools over manual shell commands or raw file reads when they fit.
- Use `database-query` for read-only SQL instead of ad hoc database access in tinker.
- Use `database-schema` to inspect table structure before writing migrations or table classes.
- Use `get-absolute-url` to resolve the correct scheme, domain, and port for project URLs. Always use this before sharing a URL with the user.
- Use `current-time` for the host clock (`App.defaultTimezone`). It returns one formatted timestamp (`Y-m-d H:i:s P`). Prefer it over shell `date` / PowerShell `Get-Date`.
{% if assist.browserLogsEnabled() or assist.browserLogsWatcherEnabled() %}
- Use `browser-logs` to read browser console logs, errors, and exceptions. Only recent entries are useful; ignore old log lines.
{% endif %}
{% endif %}

{% if assist.rulesEnabled() %}
## Project Rules
- This project contains committed, area-grouped rules in `.ai/rules` when that directory exists, including path-scoped framework guidelines under `.ai/rules/ignis`. Before you enter plan mode or create/edit any file, you MUST first: open `.ai/rules/index.md` (it maps file globs to rule files), read every rule file whose globs cover the path(s) in scope, and run `grep -rin 'keyword' .ai/rules` to catch what a path match alone misses. Do not write code until you have read and are following every matching rule. If `.ai/rules` does not exist, continue without it.

{% endif %}

## Cake Console
- Run Cake commands via the CLI (for example `{{ assist.cakeCommand('routes') }}`). Use `{{ assist.cakeCommand('') }}` to discover commands and `{{ assist.cakeCommand('[command] -h') }}` to inspect options.
- Inspect routes with `{{ assist.cakeCommand('routes') }}`.
- Read configuration from files under `config/` or use MCP `config-read` when available.

## Tinker
- Execute PHP in the application context for debugging. Do not create database records without user approval; prefer fixtures and tests.
{% if assist.hasMcpEnabled() and assist.tinkerToolEnabled() %}
- Use the `tinker` MCP tool to execute PHP instead of the CLI. It avoids shell escaping issues and runs inside the CakePHP application context.
{% else %}
- Prefer MCP `execute-tool` or existing console commands over custom one-off scripts when debugging.
{% endif %}
